==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-leave someone in the lurch.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|leave<,,left> someone in the lurch}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[abandon]] somebody; especially, to abandon somebody and [[leave]] him or her in a [[difficult]] [[situation]].
#: {{ux|en|He '''left me in the lurch''' and I had to finish the whole project by myself.}}
#* {{RQ:Butler Hudibras|part=1|page=103|passage=And though th'art of a diff'rent Church, / I will not '''leave thee in the lurch'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Kim Willsher|title=Large French Alpine ski resort to close in face of shrinking snow season|work=The Guardian|date=2024-10-07|url=https://www.theguardian.com/travel/2024/oct/07/large-french-alpine-ski-resort-to-close-in-face-of-shrinking-snow-season|issn=0261-3077|passage=Frédérique Laurence, the owner of a grocery shop in La Morte, added: “We’ve been '''left''' completely '''in the lurch'''. We still have loans to pay as we’ve only been here four years. Who will pay them? Our lives have been ruined. That’s what is going to happen to us.”}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|leave someone holding the bag}}
* {{l|en|leave someone high and dry}}
